<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Molly-Blockin.jpg" alt="Block in for portrait of Molly" width="400" height="508" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Molly Block In. 14x11, oil on linen. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This morning I did the block-in for the portrait of Molly. I used a mixture of terra rosa and raw umber applied thinly on an un-toned panel.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I will let this dry and then tone the panel before starting the final layers of the painting.&nbsp;<span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">I don't usually work in this back-to-front manner, but this morning I realized that the panel on which I intended to work was not toned. Since I prefer to work on a dry ground I decided to work out of order and do the block in first. I don't think it will make any difference to the finished work.</span></p>